block's distribution, e.g. \eqn{(\tau)^{-1/2} \sim \mathrm{Exp}(\lambda)} or
\eqn{\mathbf{Q} \sim \mathcal{W}_k(df, \mathbf{V})}; blocks without
\code{prior} (INLA's default) get none.

